  <title>Product history</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Reports</gui><gui>Products</gui><gui>Product
  history</gui></guiseq>: choose the <gui>Product</gui>, and each tab shows one
  side of its history.</p>

  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Invoices</gui></title>
    <p>Each sale, with the customer, quantity and price. Double click one to
    open the invoice as it was printed. Right click for its <gui>Invoice
    history</gui>, or select several sales and choose <gui>Selection
    statistics</gui>; see <link xref="#statistics"/>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Purchase Orders</gui></title>
    <p>Each order for it, with the vendor, price and order number. Right click
    for <gui>View attachment</gui>, the vendor's invoice.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Warranty</gui></title>
    <p>Events recorded against its serial numbers; see <link
    xref="product_serial_numbers"/>.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Manufacturing</gui></title>
    <p>Each manufacturing project that made it, with the time and employees
    it took.</p></item>
  </terms>

  <p><gui>New window</gui> opens a second product history, to compare two
  products side by side; a tab can also be dragged out into a window of its
  own. <gui>Product hub</gui> opens the <link xref="product_hub"/>,
  <gui>Refresh</gui> reloads the tabs, and <gui>Export hub</gui> exports what
  is shown; see <link xref="report_hub"/>.</p>

  <section id="statistics">
  <title>Selection statistics</title>
  <p>The <gui>Invoices product statistics</gui> window works out, over the
  sales selected: the average, smallest, largest and total invoice amount and
  the dates they span, and the average, smallest, largest and total quantity,
  price and extended price of the product's lines.</p>
  </section>

</page>
